{
  "version": "2026-10-27.1",
  "notes": [
    "Maps catalogue product names / product types and detector labels to standard product types, umbrella categories and colours.",
    "Edit this file to add brands: add keywords to an existing product type, or add a new type (and put it in type_order).",
    "Matching is on whole words after lower-casing; '&' becomes 'and'; hyphens and punctuation become spaces. Plural 's' is handled automatically.",
    "type_order matters: the first type whose keyword appears wins, so specific types (overshirt, sweatshirt, swim shorts) come before generic ones (shirt, shorts).",
    "Anything not matched stays 'unknown' on purpose. Unknown products are never offered as matches; run `python -m sceneseen match-catalogue --taxonomy-report` to list them.",
    "Product colours are read only from clear colour words; food/motif words (cherry, coffee, mint…) are deliberately not colours because printed designs use them.",
    "'short' alone is not a keyword: 'Short Sleeve Shirt' is a shirt and 'Short Socks' are socks."
  ],
